<sect1 id="EXAMPLES_DRIVERS_MEMCFG_EX1_ERROR_HANDLING_1autotoc_md428">
<title>Introduction</title>
<para>This example demonstrates error handling in case of various erroneous memory read/write operations. Error handling in case of CPU read/write violations, uncorrectable memory errors has been demonstrated. Uncorrectable memory errors &amp; violations can generate NMI interrupt</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="EXAMPLES_DRIVERS_MEMCFG_EX1_ERROR_HANDLING_1autotoc_md429">
<title>Watch  Variables</title>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>testStatusGlobal - Equivalent to <bold>TEST_PASS</bold> if test finished correctly, else the value is set to <bold>TEST_FAIL</bold> </para>
</listitem><listitem><para>errCountGlobal - Error counter</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect1>
